<title>USA: SK Telecom sells $230 mln in Yankee bonds.</title>
<headline>SK Telecom sells $230 mln in Yankee bonds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following Yankee bond offering from SK Telecom Co Ltd was priced on Thursday, according to lead manager Merrill Lynch &amp; Co.</p>
<p>The deal is SK Telecom's first Yankee bond offering.</p>
<p>SK Telecom, which recently changed its name from Korea Mobile Telecommunications, is the largest wireless telecommunciations provider in South Korea.</p>
<p>BORROWER SK TELECOM CO LTD</p>
<p>AMT $230 MLN	 COUPON 7.75 PCT   MATURITY 4/29/04</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.559  FIRST PAY DATE 10/29/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A1    YIELD 7.83 PCT    PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-PLUS    SPREAD 95 BPS     CALLABLE NON-CALLABLE</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1662))</p>
</text>
